\\viewkind4\\uc1\\pard\\sa120\\sl276\\slmult1\\lang1033\\f0\\fs22
\\pard\\sa180\\sl300\\slmult1\\b\\cf1\\fs34 AlKhair API Reference\\b0\\cf0\\fs22\\par
\\par
\\pard\\sa100\\sl276\\slmult1 This document reflects the API routes currently defined in the codebase as of 2026-06-23.\\par
\\par
\\pard\\sa140\\sl280\\slmult1\\b\\cf1\\fs28 Base URL\\b0\\cf0\\fs22\\par
\\par
\\pard\\sa100\\sl276\\slmult1 Use your application base URL, then add `/api`.\\par
\\par
\\pard\\sa100\\sl276\\slmult1 Example:\\par
\\par
\\pard\\sa60\\sl240\\slmult1\\cbpat3\\f1\\fs18
https://your-domain.com/api\\line
\\pard\\sa120\\sl276\\slmult1\\f0\\fs22\\cbpat0
\\par
\\pard\\sa100\\sl276\\slmult1 Versioned endpoints currently use:\\par
\\par
\\pard\\sa60\\sl240\\slmult1\\cbpat3\\f1\\fs18
/api/v1/...\\line
\\pard\\sa120\\sl276\\slmult1\\f0\\fs22\\cbpat0
\\par
\\pard\\sa140\\sl280\\slmult1\\b\\cf1\\fs28 Authentication\\b0\\cf0\\fs22\\par
\\par
\\pard\\sa100\\sl276\\slmult1 The API uses Laravel Sanctum bearer tokens.\\par
\\par
\\pard\\sa120\\sl276\\slmult1\\b\\fs24 Login and get token\\b0\\fs22\\par
\\par
\\pard\\sa100\\sl276\\slmult1 `POST /api/v1/auth/token`\\par
\\par
\\pard\\sa100\\sl276\\slmult1 Request:\\par
\\par
\\pard\\sa60\\sl240\\slmult1\\cbpat3\\f1\\fs18
\\{\\line
  "device_name": "android-phone",\\line
  "login": "username-or-email-or-phone",\\line
  "password": "your-password"\\line
\\}\\line
\\pard\\sa120\\sl276\\slmult1\\f0\\fs22\\cbpat0
\\par
\\pard\\sa100\\sl276\\slmult1 Successful response `201`:\\par
\\par
\\pard\\sa60\\sl240\\slmult1\\cbpat3\\f1\\fs18
\\{\\line
  "token": "plain-text-token",\\line
  "token_type": "Bearer",\\line
  "abilities": [\\line
    "students.view",\\line
    "groups.view"\\line
  ],\\line
  "user": \\{\\line
    "id": 1,\\line
    "name": "Alkhair Admin",\\line
    "username": "admin",\\line
    "roles": [\\line
      "manager"\\line
    ],\\line
    "permissions": [\\line
      "students.view",\\line
      "groups.view"\\line
    ]\\line
  \\}\\line
\\}\\line
\\pard\\sa120\\sl276\\slmult1\\f0\\fs22\\cbpat0
\\par
\\pard\\sa100\\sl276\\slmult1 Use the token in the `Authorization` header:\\par
\\par
\\pard\\sa60\\sl240\\slmult1\\cbpat3\\f1\\fs18
Authorization: Bearer plain-text-token\\line
\\pard\\sa120\\sl276\\slmult1\\f0\\fs22\\cbpat0
\\par
\\pard\\sa120\\sl276\\slmult1\\b\\fs24 Logout and revoke current token\\b0\\fs22\\par
\\par
\\pard\\sa100\\sl276\\slmult1 `DELETE /api/v1/auth/token`\\par
\\par
\\pard\\sa100\\sl276\\slmult1 Response: `204 No Content`\\par
\\par
\\pard\\sa120\\sl276\\slmult1\\b\\fs24 Authenticated user\\b0\\fs22\\par
\\par
\\pard\\sa100\\sl276\\slmult1 `GET /api/user`\\par
\\par
\\pard\\sa100\\sl276\\slmult1 Response: the authenticated Laravel user object.\\par
\\par
\\pard\\sa140\\sl280\\slmult1\\b\\cf1\\fs28 Important Auth Note\\b0\\cf0\\fs22\\par
\\par
\\pard\\sa100\\sl276\\slmult1 Current API controllers authorize requests using the logged-in user's application permissions such as `students.view`, `memorization.record`, and `attendance.student.take`.\\par
\\par
\\pard\\sa100\\sl276\\slmult1 The token `abilities` returned by the login endpoint are currently informational and are not directly checked inside these controllers with `tokenCan()`.\\par
\\par
\\pard\\sa140\\sl280\\slmult1\\b\\cf1\\fs28 Common Behavior\\b0\\cf0\\fs22\\par
\\par
\\pard\\li360\\fi-180\\sa60 \\bullet\tab Most list endpoints return Laravel paginator JSON.\\par
\\pard\\li360\\fi-180\\sa60 \\bullet\tab Common errors:\\par
\\pard\\sa100\\sl276\\slmult1   - `401` unauthenticated\\par
\\pard\\sa100\\sl276\\slmult1   - `403` forbidden or inactive account\\par
\\pard\\sa100\\sl276\\slmult1   - `422` validation or business-rule error\\par
\\pard\\li360\\fi-180\\sa60 \\bullet\tab Most protected endpoints are also scope-aware, so a user may have permission but still be blocked from records outside their scope.\\par
\\par
\\pard\\sa140\\sl280\\slmult1\\b\\cf1\\fs28 Standard Paginated Response Shape\\b0\\cf0\\fs22\\par
\\par
\\pard\\sa100\\sl276\\slmult1 List endpoints return a paginator like this:\\par
\\par
\\pard\\sa60\\sl240\\slmult1\\cbpat3\\f1\\fs18
\\{\\line
  "current_page": 1,\\line
  "data": [],\\line
  "first_page_url": "https://example.com/api/v1/students?page=1",\\line
  "from": 1,\\line
  "last_page": 3,\\line
  "last_page_url": "https://example.com/api/v1/students?page=3",\\line
  "links": [],\\line
  "next_page_url": "https://example.com/api/v1/students?page=2",\\line
  "path": "https://example.com/api/v1/students",\\line
  "per_page": 15,\\line
  "prev_page_url": null,\\line
  "to": 15,\\line
  "total": 38\\line
\\}\\line
